# v3.0.2 Harder corpus + source/chunk hygiene cases (measurement only).
#
# JSONL. Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored. Same
# RetrievalEvalCase format, plus the v3.0.2 optional fields used by the hygiene
# probe (the v3.0 scorer and v3.0.1 report-path probe ignore them):
#   expected_topic_terms      terms that legitimately belong to this topic
#   allowed_neighbour_sources sources that are on-topic neighbours, not bleed
#   expected_gap              true when no authoritative source should exist
#   query_shape               direct | value_sprint | report | decision_lookup
#   classification_notes      human context for the wrong-source taxonomy
#
# These are deliberately HARD near-neighbours that share vocabulary ("connector"
# spans Power Platform AND Copilot Studio; "DLP" spans Purview AND Power
# Platform). The probe classifies each non-expected candidate as forbidden_bleed
# / on_topic_neighbour / ambiguous / expected_gap so we can tell a real bleed
# from legitimate adjacent evidence. A clean result is an honest finding.
